  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31435382",
      "title": "Locating Users",
      "lectureOrder": 201,
      "videoOrder": 196,
      "sourceHash": "285f71cc4fb2267c8801a9c49729aa07b09ee0884b1205c711477aba3a505f78",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.54,
          "en": "How can we locate a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.54,
          "end": 7.12,
          "en": "with this Locate User button?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.12,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "Well, for this, we need to talk to the device again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 13.56,
          "en": "and ask the device for the user's position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.56,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "And this again requires the usage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 17.24,
          "en": "of native device features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.24,
          "end": 19.803,
          "en": "And again, thankfully, it is pretty easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.803,
          "end": 22.223,
          "en": "to use this functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.54,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "If we search for expo location,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 27.58,
          "en": "we find a package that helps us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.58,
          "end": 30.58,
          "en": "with the expo location package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.58,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "This is a package that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "to get geolocation information from the device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 39.179,
          "en": "so information like the current position of a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.179,
          "end": 41.14,
          "en": "Again, you find installation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.14,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "and configuration instructions here as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 46.78,
          "en": "including instructions on how to use this package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.78,
          "end": 49.453,
          "en": "if you're not using Expo, which is possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "And then we can copy this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.83,
          "end": 58.87,
          "en": "and run this expo install expo-location command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.87,
          "end": 61.693,
          "en": "in our project folder, to install this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.08,
          "end": 67.31,
          "en": "Now, installing the package is the first important step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.31,
          "end": 70.57300000000001,
          "en": "but we also need to talk about permissions again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.64,
          "end": 73.91,
          "en": "And for this, the official documentation, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.91,
          "end": 75.373,
          "en": "is the place to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.37,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "Now, location requires some permissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.78999999999999,
          "en": "especially if you need advanced forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.78999999999999,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "of this package, where you are, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 86.57,
          "en": "interested in getting the location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.57,
          "end": 88.97,
          "en": "whilst the app is in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.97,
          "end": 92.19,
          "en": "This is possible but requires special permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 95.223,
          "en": "and special configuration as you learn here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.67,
          "end": 100.09,
          "en": "Now, our app does not require the location of a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.09,
          "end": 101.86,
          "en": "whilst running in the background",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.86,
          "end": 103.55,
          "en": "so we don't need to care about this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.55,
          "end": 105.53,
          "en": "but if you are building a different kind of app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.53,
          "end": 108.193,
          "en": "you should go through these instructions as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 112.27000000000001,
          "en": "For us, this app requires some permissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.27000000000001,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "but thankfully, it will basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 119.03,
          "en": "handle those permissions automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.03,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "It will take care about these permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 122.03,
          "en": "automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.03,
          "end": 126.16,
          "en": "And therefore, we don't need to do anything special here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.16,
          "end": 127.992,
          "en": "Still, you should always have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.992,
          "end": 131.063,
          "en": "at your different configuration steps here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.22,
          "end": 134.14,
          "en": "Now, with that all set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.14,
          "end": 136.15,
          "en": "we can use this package already, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.15,
          "end": 138.27,
          "en": "We don't need any extra configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 139.103,
          "en": "as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.103,
          "end": 143.32,
          "en": "And we wanna start with this getLocationHandler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.32,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "which is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 146.623,
          "en": "when we click this Locate User button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.59,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "There we want to use some functionalities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 153.2,
          "en": "from that expo location package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.2,
          "end": 155.5,
          "en": "Therefore, I will import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.5,
          "end": 158.11,
          "en": "from expo location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.11,
          "end": 160.13,
          "en": "And that something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.13,
          "end": 164.923,
          "en": "is the getCurrentPositionAsync function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.79,
          "end": 168.17000000000002,
          "en": "That is a function exposed by the package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.17000000000002,
          "end": 172.01,
          "en": "which will give us the current position of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.01,
          "end": 175.82999999999998,
          "en": "and we can then use this position in any way we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.82999999999998,
          "end": 179.71,
          "en": "So therefore now here, in getLocationHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.71,
          "end": 182.83,
          "en": "we can call getCurrentPositionAsync.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.83,
          "end": 184.67,
          "en": "But again, it's called async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.67,
          "end": 187.86,
          "en": "because this operation will take a bit longer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.86,
          "end": 191.15,
          "en": "Locating the user is not an instant task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.15,
          "end": 193,
          "en": "though it might be really quick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193,
          "end": 194.81,
          "en": "but it can take a bit longer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.81,
          "end": 197.77,
          "en": "And therefore this actually returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 197.77,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "And therefore I will again use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "async await for convenience here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 204.56,
          "en": "Now, what we get back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.56,
          "end": 207.13,
          "en": "will be the location of the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.13,
          "end": 209.35,
          "en": "which will be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.35,
          "end": 212.21,
          "en": "And I will console log that location here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.21,
          "end": 214.82999999999998,
          "en": "so that we can see what's inside of this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 214.82999999999998,
          "end": 216.523,
          "en": "once we have the location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.59,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "Now, you can also pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 222.14,
          "en": "to getCurrentPositionAsync,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 222.14,
          "end": 224.18,
          "en": "to configure this, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 224.18,
          "end": 227.84,
          "en": "to configure the accuracy or an interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 227.84,
          "end": 230.86,
          "en": "that controls that this location is fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 230.86,
          "end": 233.41,
          "en": "every X seconds or so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 233.41,
          "end": 235.38,
          "en": "But here I don't wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 235.38,
          "end": 238.253,
          "en": "I will therefore not set any such options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 242.56,
          "en": "Now, just as before, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 242.56,
          "end": 245.293,
          "en": "we will not get the desired result though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.64,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "On Android, if I tap this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 250.81,
          "en": "it looks like nothing is happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.81,
          "end": 253.093,
          "en": "but then I get a warning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.093,
          "end": 255.09,
          "en": "And on iOS, it's the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 255.09,
          "end": 256.97,
          "en": "And we are getting these warnings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.97,
          "end": 259.1,
          "en": "because of permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 259.1,
          "end": 262.66,
          "en": "Yes, we don't need to configure anything special here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.66,
          "end": 266.38,
          "en": "We don't need to announce as part of the app configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.38,
          "end": 268.81,
          "en": "that we are using the location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.81,
          "end": 272.87,
          "en": "because Expo or this package will do this for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 272.87,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "but we still need to ask for permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 276.75,
          "en": "as part of our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276.75,
          "end": 279.61,
          "en": "just as we did it with the image picker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 279.61,
          "end": 281.8,
          "en": "There we also had to ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 281.8,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "that we have appropriate permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 286.34000000000003,
          "en": "For Android, we didn't have to do it there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 286.34000000000003,
          "end": 287.71,
          "en": "but for iOS, we did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 287.71,
          "end": 289.4,
          "en": "Now, for the location,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 289.4,
          "end": 291.82,
          "en": "it is required for both devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 291.82,
          "end": 294.6,
          "en": "for both operating systems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 294.6,
          "end": 297.25,
          "en": "Now, the approach is the same as before though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 297.25,
          "end": 299.40999999999997,
          "en": "We can add our async helper function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 299.40999999999997,
          "end": 301.453,
          "en": "that could be called verifyPermissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 302.74,
          "end": 305.04,
          "en": "And in there, we again wanna check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 307.13,
          "en": "if we already have the permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 307.13,
          "end": 309.57,
          "en": "and request it if we don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 309.57,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "Now just as with the expo image picker package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 314.46,
          "en": "we can use a special hook for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 314.46,
          "end": 317.1,
          "en": "the useForegroundPermissions hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 317.1,
          "end": 319.39,
          "en": "which we can execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 319.39,
          "end": 323.05,
          "en": "and which gives us an array with two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 323.05,
          "end": 324.51,
          "en": "The first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 329.39,
          "en": "is locationPermissionInformation object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 329.39,
          "end": 332.64,
          "en": "The second element is a requestPermission function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 332.64,
          "end": 335.61,
          "en": "So it has the same functionality as the camera,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 335.61,
          "end": 337.543,
          "en": "the useCameraPermissions hook did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 338.62,
          "end": 340.81,
          "en": "Now inside of verifyPermissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 340.81,
          "end": 344.17,
          "en": "we can then use this information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 344.17,
          "end": 347.31,
          "en": "And we can really copy the code from the image picker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 347.31,
          "end": 349.63,
          "en": "And we could therefore, of course, also kind of build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 349.63,
          "end": 353.84000000000003,
          "en": "a reusable shared component or helper function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 353.84000000000003,
          "end": 357.44,
          "en": "But I will just copy it, copy it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 357.44,
          "end": 359.89,
          "en": "from image picker into verifyPermissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 359.89,
          "end": 361.86,
          "en": "in the location picker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 365.06,
          "en": "But of course, instead of the cameraPermissionInformation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 365.06,
          "end": 368.38,
          "en": "we have the locationPermissionInformation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 368.38,
          "end": 370.41,
          "en": "It has the same status field though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 370.41,
          "end": 372.863,
          "en": "So that does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 373.95,
          "end": 375.83,
